# The one list of fleet.env settings. `fleet-config check` reads it.
#
# GENERATED in part by scripts/settings-manifest --write: `section`, `readers`,
# `code-default` (only when every reader states the same one),
# `default-conflict` and `empty-differs` (an empty value means something other
# than unset, so it is a setting, not a removable line) come from the code
# and are rewritten.
# Kept by hand, and preserved on --write:
#   secret:    yes - a credential; step 2 of the fleet.env split moves these
#              into systemd credentials, one lane at a time
#   required:  always | if KEY=VALUE  - fleet-config check reports it missing
#   default:   VALUE - what the code uses when the key is unset; a setting
#              equal to it can be removed. Overrides code-default when both
#              are present, for defaults the scanner cannot see
#   note:      one line for a person
# task check fails when this file is out of date with the code: run
# scripts/settings-manifest --write and review the diff.

